course: dictionary
lesson: 12225
title: Consensus: when most people agree
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Consensus is a noun. It means agreement among all or most people in a group. You can reach a consensus, which means a group has decided together. «The class reached a consensus: the trip would be to the science museum.» Everyone, or almost everyone, agreed.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like «all», «most» and «agreed» point to a consensus. «There was no consensus, so we took a vote.» Here, the group did not agree, so "no consensus" means people disagree.
explain: Experts use the word too. The scientific consensus is the view that most experts reach after studying the evidence. «Scientists have a strong consensus on this.» It is not one person's idea. It is what most experts agree on after checking the facts.
fact: Consensus means agreement among all or most people in a group.
fact: Consensus is a noun, so you can say "a consensus" or "reach a consensus".
fact: «Reach a consensus» means a group agrees together on a decision.
fact: «There is no consensus» means people disagree.
fact: The scientific consensus is the general view of most experts after studying the evidence.
exercise: «The class reached a consensus on where to go for the trip.» What does consensus mean here? | A short test at the end of the day | A list of rules written by the teacher | A loud argument with shouting | *Agreement among most people in the group
exercise: «There was no consensus, so the school council had a vote.» What does this sentence tell you? | Everyone agreed straight away | The vote was cancelled because everyone was happy | The council was closed for the day | *The people did not agree
exercise: «Scientists have a general consensus after studying the evidence.» What is a scientific consensus? | *The view that most experts agree on | One scientist's private guess | A new invention | A type of experiment
test: «We need to build a consensus before we choose the class pet.» What does build a consensus mean? | Make a plan with the pet shop | Buy a bigger cage | Ask the teacher to decide alone | *Help the group reach agreement
test: Which word means nearly the same as consensus? | *Agreement | Argument | Mistake | Silence
exam: Maya says, «The whole group has reached a consensus.» Which is the best meaning? | *Most people in the group agree | Nobody has spoken yet | Only Maya agrees | The group is arguing and will not stop
